course: dictionary
lesson: 8945
title: Silkworm and word parts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A silkworm is a word made of two smaller words: silk and worm. Even if you have never met one, the parts give you clues. Silk is a fine, smooth thread, and a worm is a small creature, so a silkworm is a creature that makes silk thread.
explain: «The Chinese learned to make silk from silkworm cocoons.» A cocoon is a case that wraps around an animal. The sentence tells you silkworms make cocoons, and that people take silk from them. When a word is new, read the words around it and look for the parts you already know.
explain: «The Chinese learned to make silk from the cocoons of silkworms that eat mulberry leaves.» This sentence gives you more clues about what a silkworm does and eats. Use the parts of the word, then the sentence around it, and check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: A silkworm is the caterpillar of the silk moth.
fact: A silkworm spins a cocoon of fine silk thread, and people use this thread to make silk cloth.
fact: «Silkworm» is a noun. You can say «a silkworm» or «silkworms».
fact: Silkworms eat only mulberry leaves.
fact: China kept the making of silk secret for centuries, and silk was traded along the Silk Road.
exercise: «The Chinese learned to make silk from silkworm cocoons.» What is a silkworm? | A kind of silk cloth | A tree that grows mulberries | *The caterpillar of the silk moth | A moth that eats leaves
exercise: «The Chinese learned to make silk from the cocoons of silkworms that eat mulberry leaves.» What do silkworms eat? | *Mulberry leaves | Grass and flowers | Silk thread | Apples and pears
exercise: Jayden says silkworm is made of two smaller words. Which two? | Silver and worm | Sick and worm | Silk and moth | *Silk and worm
test: What kind of word is silkworm? | *A noun | A place name | A verb | An adjective
test: What do people use the silk thread from a cocoon for? | *Making silk cloth | Building houses | Making paper | Cooking food
exam: Which statement is true? | Silkworms spin cloth straight from their mouths onto a loom | *A silkworm is the caterpillar of the silk moth | Silkworms are a kind of mulberry tree | Silk comes from spiders only
